    "Test Case Name": "pcie0_dbi_dsp_reg_wr_rd_test",
    "Test Description": "Validate PCIe DBI/PL register blocks by checking default reset values and verifying masked write/read integrity across capability, AER, MSI, iATU, and Link Control registers. Certain status/next-pointer and debug registers are excluded from default checks. The test writes multiple data patterns to writable fields, reads back, and compares against expected values considering read/write masks and preserved reset bits.",
    "Meta Test Description": "The test iterates over CNT=775 DBI/PL register addresses (addr_array). Phase 1: Default check (chk_rst_val) skips any address with read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 and also skips three specific addresses (mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF). For each remaining address, it reads data_rd=read_reg(addr_array[i]) and compares with default_value_array[i]; increments def_fail_cnt on mismatch. Phase 2: Write/Read check (chk_rd_wr) runs for six data patterns: 0xffffffff, 0xaaaaaaaa, 0x55555555, 0x00000000, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xffff0000. Write phase: for each i, if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000, skip; else write_reg(addr_array[i], data_wr). Read/compare phase: skip if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0x00000000 or read_mask_array[i]==0x00000000; otherwise read data_rd, compute wr_n=(write_mask_array[i]^0xffffffff), exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); on mismatch wr_fail_cnt++. End: finish(1) if def_fail_cnt>0 or wr_fail_cnt>0; else finish(0). soft_reset_chk writes SOFT_RST_REG_DATA to SOFT_RST_REG_ADDRESS and restores it after delays, but is not invoked.",
    "Speed": "NA",
    "Mode": "Polling",
    "Memory Start Offset": "NA",
    "Memory End Offset": "NA",
    "Remarks": "Non-readable and non-writable registers are skipped per masks; additional exclusions are applied via a skip list. Default-value checks exclude the capability next-pointer, combined device control/status, and PL debug registers. Readbacks must reflect only writable, readable fields while non-writable bits remain at reset values.",
    "Test Steps / Procedure": "1) Load the DBI/PL address, default, and mask tables. 2) Validate default reset values for all readable registers, excluding the capability next-pointer, device control/status, and PL debug registers. 3) For six data patterns, write all writable, non-excluded registers, then read back only those that are readable and writable. 4) Verify each readback matches the masked expectation, preserving reset-only bits. 5) Pass if no mismatches are detected; otherwise fail.",
    "Meta Test Steps / Procedure": "1) chk_rst_val(): for i=0..CNT-1: if read_mask_array[i]==0 continue; if addr in {mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF} continue; data_rd=read_reg(addr_array[i]); compare to default_value_array[i]; on mismatch def_fail_cnt++. 2) chk_rd_wr(): patterns={0xffffffff,0xaaaaaaaa,0x55555555,0x00000000,0xA5A5A5A5,0xffff0000}. For each data_wr: (a) writes: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0 continue; else write_reg(addr_array[i], data_wr). (b) reads: if skip_array[i]==1 or write_mask_array[i]==0 or read_mask_array[i]==0 continue; else data_rd=read_reg(addr_array[i]); wr_n=(write_mask_array[i]^0xffffffff); exp_val=((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | (wr_n & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])); if data_rd!=exp_val wr_fail_cnt++. 3) If counters >0 finish(1) else finish(0). 4) soft_reset_chk() (not called): save default; write SOFT_RST_REG_DATA; wait; restore; wait.",
    "Impacted Registers": "DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, DBI_DSP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, DBI_DSP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, DBI_DSP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG, DBI_DSP_AER_EXT_CAP_HDR_OFF, DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL2_DEVICE_STATUS2_REG",
    "Meta Impacted Registers": "mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_CAP_ID_NXT_PTR_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL_DEVICE_STATUS, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_PL_DEBUG1_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_MSI_CTRL_INT_0_EN_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_IATU_REGION_CTRL_1_OFF_OUTBOUND_0, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_LINK_CONTROL_LINK_STATUS_REG, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_AER_EXT_CAP_HDR_OFF, mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_DEVICE_CONTROL2_DEVICE_STATUS2_REG",
    "Validation / Acceptance Criteria": "PASS if all eligible readable registers match their reset values (excluding specified exceptions) and all eligible readable+writable registers match masked expectations across all data patterns; otherwise FAIL.",
    "Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria": "Default: require data_rd == default_value_array[i] for i with read_mask_array[i]!=0 and addr not in excluded set. Write/read: for each pattern and i with skip_array[i]==0, read_mask_array[i]!=0, write_mask_array[i]!=0, require data_rd == ((data_wr & read_mask_array[i] & write_mask_array[i]) | ((~write_mask_array[i]) & read_mask_array[i] & default_value_array[i])). Final: finish(0) iff def_fail_cnt==0 && wr_fail_cnt==0; else finish(1).",
    "Code Generation (Required / Not)": "Not",
