    "Test Case Name": "pcie_cfg_wr_rd_test",
    "Test Description": "Program coherency control fields in the PCIe DBI for multiple instances, poll SII status until the link is ready, then perform PCIe configuration space BAR sizing and programming and enable Command register fields. Use a handshake register to synchronize completion. Validate by successful polling exit and final synchronization.",
    "Meta Test Description": "Optionally trigger link training via compile-time selects (DMx_*). Program DBI coherency fields by modifying bitfields across several ranges in DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF for PCIe0 and PCIe1, with multiple passes and waits. Poll SII0 status at offset 0xC0 until (value & 0xD1)==0xD1; if DM1_RC is enabled, similarly poll SII1. Write 0x11111111 to 0xE6004100 then delay. For DM0_RC: call mem_base_program_dm0_x4(); read initial config space headers via read_pcie_slv0_reg() loop; write 0xFFFFFFFF to BAR offsets 0x10..0x24; read back; program BARs to {0x0,0x4,0x20000000,0x40000000,0x60000000,0x80000000}; enable Memory/IO/Bus Master by writing 0x7 to offset 0x4. For DM1_RC: analogous sequence using read_pcie_slv1_reg()/write_pcie_slv1_reg(). Finally, poll read_reg(0xE6004100) until it equals 0x12345678; then finish(0).",
    "Speed": "NA",
    "Mode": "Polling",
    "Memory Start Offset": "0xE6004100",
    "Memory End Offset": "0xE6004100",
    "Remarks": "Requires link readiness indicated by SII status polling. Coherency fields are adjusted in the coherency control register. External environment must drive the handshake location to 0x12345678 to complete the test.",
    "Test Steps / Procedure": "1) If enabled, initiate link training for the selected PCIe instances. 2) Configure coherency settings by updating fields in the coherency control register for each PCIe instance. 3) Poll SII status to confirm link readiness before proceeding. 4) For each enabled Root Complex instance, initialize memory base and read initial configuration headers. 5) Perform BAR sizing writes and reads, then program BAR base addresses and enable Memory/IO/Bus Master in the Command register. 6) Wait for the external completion handshake to reach 0x12345678, then declare PASS.",
    "Meta Test Steps / Procedure": "1) write_reg(0xE6004100,0x0). Optional: link_training_dm0_x4 / link_training_dm1_x4 under compile-time macros. 2) For PCIe0 and PCIe1: rd_wr_data1=read_reg(mizar_PCIE{0,1}_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF); rd_wr_data1=set_data() over ranges {11..14,3..6} and later {27..30,19..22}; write back; repeat after wait to combine all fields. 3) Poll: while ((read_sii0_reg(0xC0) & 0xD1) != 0xD1) continue; if DM1_RC enabled, similarly poll read_sii1_reg(0xC0). 4) write_reg(0xE6004100,0x11111111); wait_on(15000). 5) If DM0_RC: mem_base_program_dm0_x4(); for i=0..9: read_pcie_slv0_reg(i*0x4); write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x10..0x24,0xFFFFFFFF); read back 0x10..0x24; then write BAR values {0x0,0x4,0x20000000,0x40000000,0x60000000,0x80000000}; write_pcie_slv0_reg(0x4,0x7). 6) If DM1_RC: analogous with *_slv1_* accessors. 7) Poll read_reg(0xE6004100) until 0x12345678; finish(0).",
    "Impacted Registers": "DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF",
    "Meta Impacted Registers": "mizar_PCIE0_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF, mizar_PCIE1_DBI_DSP_COHERENCY_CONTROL_3_OFF",
    "Validation / Acceptance Criteria": "PASS if SII status polling completes (link ready) and the final handshake value at 0xE6004100 transitions to 0x12345678, resulting in test completion without error.",
    "Meta Validation / Acceptance Criteria": "Require loop exit when (read_sii0_reg(0xC0) & 0xD1) == 0xD1 (and similarly for SII1 if enabled). Require final loop exit when read_reg(0xE6004100) == 0x12345678; then finish(0).",
    "Code Generation (Required / Not)": "Not",
